                    <tr>
                      <td>{s.n}</td>
                      <td>{s.site}</td>
                      <td>{s.dr}</td>
                      <td>{s.da}</td>
                      <td>{s.pa}</td>
                      <td>{s.ur}</td>
                      <td>{s.traffic}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))}
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </figure>

            <h2 id="pitch">The pitch that works for regional editors</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Lead with the country or city.</strong> "What the new Indonesian data law means for SaaS" or "Manila's fintech scene by the numbers" earns the read.</li>
              <li><strong>Show you know the market.</strong> Local sources, local data, an understanding of the regulatory context.</li>
              <li><strong>Pitch the desk.</strong> "For your startup coverage" or "for the analysis section" shows you read the outlet.</li>
              <li><strong>Bring the assets.</strong> A data set, a chart, an executive quote, a country-by-country table.</li>
              <li><strong>Match the format.</strong> News wants a tight story. Business outlets want a structured analysis. Travel media want a practical guide.</li>
              <li><strong>Disclose any client or brand tie</strong> up front.</li>
            </ol>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>The test:</strong> would this editor run the piece if you had nothing to sell in the region? If yes, pitch it.</p></div>

            <h2 id="mistakes">What not to do</h2>
            <ul class="check-list">
              <li>Send a US or Europe piece with a country name swapped in.</li>
              <li>Pitch a national daily a "guest post." That format does not exist there.</li>
              <li>Treat the whole region as one market. Each country's rules, press and audience are different.</li>
              <li>Put exact-match anchors on links back to your product.</li>
              <li>Chase titles that have closed. Check the site is still publishing.</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="callout"><p><strong>Bottom line:</strong> a few placements on active regional outlets with a genuine country angle will move rankings and pipeline more than a long list of links, some pointing at titles that no longer exist. Use this list to find your few.</p></div>
          </div>

          <aside class="article-toc">
